<title>ITALY: Olivetti suspended limit down again.</title>
<headline>Olivetti suspended limit down again.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Italian information technology group Olivetti were suspended limit down yet again on the Milan stock market on Tuesday after touching a 10 percent fluctuation limit.</p>
<p>Stock market authorities said a new attempt to resume trading would be made at 1308 GMT.</p>
<p>This is the fifth time the stock has triggered automatic suspension in the day. Due to the nature of pre-trade price matching it has only managed to resume normal trading three times.  </p>
<p>The stock is now registering the last price of 467 lire per share, just above its record low set earlier at 465 lire.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
